# Ask for Live Logs Before Diagnosing Bugs

If you are not 100% certain about the root cause of a bug — even the slightest doubt — ask the user for live logs before proposing or applying a fix.

Do NOT assume the cause from code alone when runtime behaviour might differ. Always say:

> "Can you share the live logs for this request? That will confirm the root cause before I make any changes."

The user can pull logs from Cloudflare Workers Observability (Query Builder → filter by trigger path).

Only skip asking if the bug is fully deterministic from static analysis with zero ambiguity (e.g. a TypeScript compile error or a clearly wrong constant).
